{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Technical Design: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\n     2\t\n     3\t## Purpose\n     4\t\n     5\tThis document translates Epic 7 into an implementable design for canonical\n     6\tprocess archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\n     7\tIt is the implementation blueprint for preserving finalized low-level process\n     8\thistory while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\n     9\tcanonical truth.\n    10\t\n    11\t| Audience | Value |\n    12\t|----------|-------|\n    13\t| Reviewers | Validate that archive work follows the core platform architecture |\n    14\t| Developers | Know which routes, services, Convex functions, contracts, and tests to build |\n    15\t| Story Tech Sections | Reuse interfaces, flow designs, TC mappings, and chunk breakdowns |\n    16\t\n    17\tRelated documents:\n    18\t\n    19\t- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\n    20\t- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\n    21\t- Architecture: `docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md`\n    22\t- Epic 6 tech design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md`\n    23\t\n    24\tOutput configuration: Config A. Epic 7 gets this `tech-design.md` and a separate\n    25\t`test-plan.md`. The work crosses live process, Fastify, Convex, and client read\n    26\tsurfaces, but the archive domain is coherent enough for one index document.\n    27\t\n    28\t## Spec Validation\n    29\t\n    30\tEpic 7 is implementation-ready. It is scoped to canonical finalized archive\n    31\tentries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\n    32\tbounded degraded reads. It explicitly avoids model-generated summaries,\n    33\texternal-source attachment, and replacing the existing live WebSocket/upsert\n    34\tmodel.\n    35\t\n    36\t| Issue | Spec Location | Resolution | Status |\n    37\t|-------|---------------|------------|--------|\n    38\t| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\n    39\t| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\n    40\t| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\n    41\t| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\n    42\t| Provenance links must not duplicate Epic 5/6 ownership logic | AC-6.x | Design stores nullable related ids and enriches through existing artifact/source services at read time. Archive entries remain visible when enrichment degrades. | Resolved |\n    43\t\n    44\tNo design-time deviation from the PRD or architecture is required. Fastify owns\n    45\tarchive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\n    46\tview refresh. Convex owns durable append/read storage, ordering, idempotency\n    47\tguards, and optional cached projection records.\n    48\t\n    49\t## Tech Design Questions Answered\n    50\t\n    51\t| # | Epic Question | Design Answer |\n    52\t|---|---------------|---------------|\n    53\t| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\n    54\t| 2 | What compatibility mapping bridges `processHistoryItems` and live updates, and is migration/backfill in scope? | Add compatibility helpers that map new finalized archive entries to existing process-history surfaces where needed. Existing `processHistoryItems` remain the legacy presentation read model. No historical migration/backfill is in scope for Epic 7. |\n    55\t| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\n    56\t| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\n    57\t| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\n    58\t| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\n    59\t| 7 | How should source/artifact provenance link without duplicating ownership logic? | Archive entries store nullable related ids (`relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`). Read services enrich from existing artifact/source services and degrade per entry when related records are unavailable. |\n    60\t| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\n    61\t| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\n    62\t\n    63\t## Context\n    64\t\n    65\tThe platform already has process history, but it is presentation history. The\n    66\tcurrent `processHistoryItems` table supports the process work surface and live\n    67\thistory upserts with a smaller vocabulary: `user_message`, `process_message`,\n    68\t`progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and\n    69\t`process_event`. That is useful UI state, but it is not the full-fidelity\n    70\tarchive the PRD requires for long-horizon context management.\n    71\t\n    72\tEpic 7 introduces canonical archive truth without tearing out the live surface.\n    73\tFastify still normalizes runtime events into typed WebSocket upserts for active\n    74\tUI state. Separately, completed process objects are finalized into archive\n    75\tentries at low-level grain. This preserves the active interaction model while\n    76\tmaking later turn/query/chunk work rebuildable from a stable durable record.\n    77\t\n    78\tThe design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\n    79\tstructural views help later context-management work, but they do not replace\n    80\tarchive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\n    81\tarchive. If derivation fails, the archive remains readable. That property is\n    82\tmore important than early summarization convenience.\n    83\t\n    84\tEpic 7 also consumes Epic 5 and Epic 6 provenance without taking ownership of\n    85\tthose domains. Artifact versions keep producing-process provenance in the\n    86\tartifact/version model. Source provenance keeps repository identity in Epic 6\n    87\trecords. Archive entries may link to those records and show related context, but\n    88\tthey do not redefine artifact ownership or source attachment lifecycle.\n    89\t\n    90\t## System View\n    91\t\n    92\t### Top-Tier Surfaces\n    93\t\n    94\t| Surface | Source | This Epic's Role |\n    95\t|---------|--------|------------------|\n    96\t| Processes | Core architecture | Finalization points and archive read access live under one project/process |\n    97\t| Archive | Core architecture | Primary Epic 7 domain; owns canonical entries and rebuildable projections |\n    98\t| Projects | Core architecture | Project/process access gates archive reads |\n    99\t| Artifacts | Core architecture | Provides related artifact-version context during archive reads |\n   100\t| Sources | Core architecture + Epic 6 | Provides related source provenance context during archive reads |\n   101\t| Client | Core architecture | Adds process-surface entry points for archive, turn, and structural-view reads |\n   102\t\n   103\t### Runtime Flow\n   104\t\n   105\t```mermaid\n   106\tflowchart LR\n   107\t    EXEC[Process/runtime completion points]\n   108\t    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\n   109\t    STORE[PlatformStore]\n   110\t    X[(Convex Archive Tables)]\n   111\t    READ[ArchiveReadService]\n   112\t    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\n   113\t    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\n   114\t    API[Fastify archive routes]\n   115\t    UI[Client process/archive UI]\n   116\t\n   117\t    EXEC --> FINAL\n   118\t    FINAL --> STORE\n   119\t    STORE --> X\n   120\t    UI --> API\n   121\t    API --> READ\n   122\t    READ --> STORE\n   123\t    READ --> DERIVE\n   124\t    DERIVE --> VIEWS\n   125\t    VIEWS --> STORE\n   126\t```\n   127\t\n   128\tThe append path is narrow and trusted. Fastify calls\n   129\t`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\n   130\tnormalizes the finalized object into canonical archive entry shape and asks\n   131\t`PlatformStore` to append it. Convex assigns sequence and enforces idempotency.\n   132\t\n   133\tThe read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\n   134\tentries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\n   135\tstructural views. These services read durable archive data and enrich related\n   136\tartifact/source context independently. A related-context failure degrades one\n   137\tentry or view rather than hiding the archive.\n   138\t\n   139\t## Decisions\n   140\t\n   141\t| Decision | Rationale | Consequence |\n   142\t|----------|-----------|-------------|\n   143\t| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\n   144\t| Fastify owns finalization policy | Architecture says Fastify owns orchestration and live-event normalization | Convex append functions are durable primitives with validators and idempotency guards |\n   145\t| Convex assigns `sequence` atomically | Stable ordering must survive same timestamps and retries | Append mutation computes next sequence per process |\n   146\t| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\n   147\t| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\n   148\t| Derived views are structural only | Prevents scope creep into summarization | `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` contain boundaries/provenance, not generated summaries |\n   149\t| No historical migration/backfill | Epic 7 is forward canonicalization plus compatibility bridge | Existing `processHistoryItems` remain visible, but old rows are not retroactively canonical |\n   150\t\n   151\t## Module Boundaries\n   152\t\n   153\t### File Architecture\n   154\t\n   155\t```\n   156\tconvex/\n   157\t├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\n   158\t├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\n   159\t├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\n   160\t└── schema.ts                                 # MODIFIED: archive tables and indexes\n   161\t\n   162\tapps/platform/shared/contracts/\n   163\t├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\n   164\t├── process-work-surface.ts                   # MODIFIED: optional archive entry points/actions in process surface contract\n   165\t└── index.ts                                  # MODIFIED: exports\n   166\t\n   167\tapps/platform/server/schemas/\n   168\t└── archive.ts                                # NEW: Fastify route schemas for archive APIs\n   169\t\n   170\tapps/platform/server/routes/\n   171\t└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\n   172\t\n   173\tapps/platform/server/services/archive/\n   174\t├── archive-finalization.service.ts           # NEW: finalized-object to archive-entry mapping\n   175\t├── archive-read.service.ts                   # NEW: archive read/enrichment/degraded-state orchestration\n   176\t├── turn-derivation.service.ts                # NEW: deterministic turn derivation and rebuild\n   177\t├── derived-archive-view.service.ts           # NEW: structural view creation/read/refresh\n   178\t└── process-history-compat.service.ts         # NEW: bridge archive entries to existing history surface when needed\n   179\t\n   180\tapps/platform/server/services/projects/\n   181\t└── platform-store.ts                         # MODIFIED: archive append/read/projection methods\n   182\t\n   183\tapps/platform/server/services/processes/\n   184\t├── environment/process-environment.service.ts # MODIFIED: call finalization for execution/tool/process events\n   185\t├── process-response.service.ts               # MODIFIED: archive accepted user responses\n   186\t└── live/process-live-normalizer.ts           # UNCHANGED: live upserts remain current-object transport\n   187\t\n   188\tapps/platform/client/features/processes/\n   189\t├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\n   190\t├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\n   191\t└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\n   192\t\n   193\tapps/platform/client/app/\n   194\t└── bootstrap.ts                              # MODIFIED: route archive actions to process/archive surfaces\n   195\t\n   196\ttests/\n   197\t├── fixtures/archive.ts                       # NEW: archive/turn/view fixtures\n   198\t├── service/server/archive-api.test.ts        # NEW: Fastify archive route tests\n   199\t├── service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts # NEW: finalization and idempotency tests\n   200\t├── service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts    # NEW: deterministic turn derivation tests\n   201\t├── service/client/archive-section.test.ts    # NEW: client archive rendering tests\n   202\t├── service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts # NEW: turn surface rendering tests\n   203\t└── service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts # NEW: derived-view UI tests\n   204\t```\n   205\t\n   206\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\n   207\t\n   208\t| Module | Status | Responsibility | Dependencies | ACs Covered |\n   209\t|--------|--------|----------------|--------------|-------------|\n   210\t| `convex/archiveEntries.ts` | New | Append/read canonical entries, sequence assignment, idempotency guard, pagination | Convex schema | AC-1.x, AC-2.3, AC-3.x, AC-7.3 |\n   211\t| `convex/archiveTurns.ts` | New | Store rebuildable cached turns | Convex schema | AC-4.x, AC-7.1 |\n   212\t| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\n   213\t| `ArchiveFinalizationService` | New | Map completed process objects to archive entries; exclude deltas/partials | PlatformStore | AC-1.x, AC-2.x |\n   214\t| `ArchiveReadService` | New | Read archive entries, enforce access via routes/services, enrich related context, degrade locally | PlatformStore, artifact/source services | AC-3.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\n   215\t| `TurnDerivationService` | New | Deterministically derive/rebuild turns from archive entries | PlatformStore | AC-4.x |\n   216\t| `DerivedArchiveViewService` | New | Build/read non-summarizing structural views | PlatformStore, TurnDerivationService | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\n   217\t| `ProcessHistoryCompatService` | New | Bridge archive entries to existing history surfaces without migration | ArchiveReadService | A7, Story 0 |\n   218\t| `registerArchiveRoutes` | New | Fastify entry points, auth/access, request/response validation | ProcessAccessService, archive services | AC-3.x through AC-7.x |\n   219\t| Client archive sections | New | Render archive, turns, structural views, empty/degraded states | Shared contracts/API client | AC-3.x, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\n   220\t\n   221\t## Data Model\n   222\t\n   223\t### Convex `archiveEntries`\n   224\t\n   225\t```typescript\n   226\texport const archiveEntryKindValidator = v.union(\n   227\t  v.literal('user_message'),\n   228\t  v.literal('model_message'),\n   229\t  v.literal('reasoning'),\n   230\t  v.literal('script_emission'),\n   231\t  v.literal('tool_call'),\n   232\t  v.literal('tool_result'),\n   233\t  v.literal('process_event'),\n   234\t);\n   235\t\n   236\texport const archiveEntriesTableFields = {\n   237\t  projectId: v.string(),\n   238\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\n   239\t  entryKind: archiveEntryKindValidator,\n   240\t  sequence: v.number(),\n   241\t  lifecycleState: v.literal('finalized'),\n   242\t  finalizationKey: v.string(),\n   243\t  sourceObjectId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   244\t  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   245\t  bodyData: v.union(\n   246\t    v.object({\n   247\t      jsonText: v.string(),\n   248\t    }),\n   249\t    v.null(),\n   250\t  ),\n   251\t  bodyFormat: v.union(v.literal('plain_text'), v.literal('markdown'), v.literal('structured'), v.literal('none')),\n   252\t  relatedArtifactVersionId: v.union(v.id('artifactVersions'), v.null()),\n   253\t  relatedSourceProvenanceId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   254\t  relatedToolCallId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   255\t  entryStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n   256\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   257\t  recordedAt: v.string(),\n   258\t};\n   259\t```\n   260\t\n   261\tIndexes:\n   262\t\n   263\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n   264\t|-------|--------|---------|\n   265\t| `by_processId_sequence` | `processId`, `sequence` | Canonical archive pagination |\n   266\t| `by_processId_finalizationKey` | `processId`, `finalizationKey` | Idempotency guard |\n   267\t| `by_projectId_processId_recordedAt` | `projectId`, `processId`, `recordedAt` | Project/process scoped diagnostics |\n   268\t\n   269\t`appendArchiveEntry` performs the final idempotency check and sequence assignment\n   270\tinside one Convex mutation. Fastify can preflight finalization keys, but Convex\n   271\towns the atomic guard.\n   272\t\n   273\t### Convex `archiveTurns`\n   274\t\n   275\t```typescript\n   276\texport const archiveTurnsTableFields = {\n   277\t  projectId: v.string(),\n   278\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\n   279\t  turnId: v.string(),\n   280\t  turnIndex: v.number(),\n   281\t  archiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\n   282\t  startedAt: v.string(),\n   283\t  endedAt: v.string(),\n   284\t  turnStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n   285\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   286\t  rebuiltAt: v.string(),\n   287\t};\n   288\t```\n   289\t\n   290\tIndexes:\n   291\t\n   292\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n   293\t|-------|--------|---------|\n   294\t| `by_processId_turnId` | `processId`, `turnId` | Stable turn lookups across rebuilds |\n   295\t| `by_processId_turnIndex` | `processId`, `turnIndex` | Turn pagination and stable ordering |\n   296\t\n   297\tTurns are cached because bounded reads matter for long processes. The cache is\n   298\tnot canonical. `TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` must upsert turns by stable\n   299\t`turnId` (`${processId}:turn:${turnIndex}`) so derived-view provenance stays\n   300\tvalid across rebuilds.\n   301\t\n   302\t### Convex `derivedArchiveViews`\n   303\t\n   304\t```typescript\n   305\texport const derivedArchiveViewsTableFields = {\n   306\t  projectId: v.string(),\n   307\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\n   308\t  viewKind: v.union(v.literal('turn_range'), v.literal('chunk_candidate')),\n   309\t  startTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\n   310\t  endTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\n   311\t  sourceTurnIds: v.array(v.string()),\n   312\t  sourceArchiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\n   313\t  title: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   314\t  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   315\t  viewStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n   316\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n   317\t  updatedAt: v.string(),\n   318\t};\n   319\t```\n   320\t\n   321\tIndexes:\n   322\t\n   323\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n   324\t|-------|--------|---------|\n   325\t| `by_processId_updatedAt` | `processId`, `updatedAt` | Derived-view reads |\n   326\t\n   327\tFor `turn_range`, `startTurnIndex` and `endTurnIndex` are required by Fastify\n   328\tvalidation before persistence. For `chunk_candidate`, the view must include\n   329\tsource turn ids and source archive entry ids; it must not include generated\n   330\tsummary content. Derived-view rows may be deleted and recreated from turns; this\n   331\tdoes not affect canonical archive entries.\n   332\t\n   333\tThe array fields in `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are intentionally\n   334\tbounded. Epic 7 limits turn rows to one process turn and derived views to small\n   335\tstructural groupings, not unbounded child lists. Long-process pagination stays\n   336\tat the archive-entry and turn level rather than trying to persist one giant\n   337\tderived record.\n   338\t\n   339\t## API Contracts\n   340\t\n   341\tShared contracts live in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts`.\n   342\t\n   343\t```typescript\n   344\texport type ArchiveEntryKind =\n   345\t  | 'user_message'\n   346\t  | 'model_message'\n   347\t  | 'reasoning'\n   348\t  | 'script_emission'\n   349\t  | 'tool_call'\n   350\t  | 'tool_result'\n   351\t  | 'process_event';\n   352\t\n   353\texport interface ArchiveEntry {\n   354\t  archiveEntryId: string;\n   355\t  projectId: string;\n   356\t  processId: string;\n   357\t  entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n   358\t  sequence: number;\n   359\t  lifecycleState: 'finalized';\n   360\t  finalizationKey: string;\n   361\t  sourceObjectId: string | null;\n   362\t  bodyText: string | null;\n   363\t  bodyData: { jsonText: string } | null;\n   364\t  bodyFormat: 'plain_text' | 'markdown' | 'structured' | 'none';\n   365\t  relatedArtifactVersionId: string | null;\n   366\t  relatedSourceProvenanceId: string | null;\n   367\t  relatedToolCallId: string | null;\n   368\t  entryStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n   369\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n   370\t  recordedAt: string;\n   371\t}\n   372\t\n   373\texport interface ArchivePage {\n   374\t  entries: ArchiveEntry[];\n   375\t  page: { cursor: string | null; nextCursor: string | null; hasMore: boolean };\n   376\t}\n   377\t\n   378\texport interface DerivedTurn {\n   379\t  turnId: string;\n   380\t  processId: string;\n   381\t  turnIndex: number;\n   382\t  archiveEntryIds: string[];\n   383\t  startedAt: string;\n   384\t  endedAt: string;\n   385\t  turnStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n   386\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n   387\t}\n   388\t\n   389\texport interface DerivedArchiveView {\n   390\t  derivedViewId: string;\n   391\t  processId: string;\n   392\t  viewKind: 'turn_range' | 'chunk_candidate';\n   393\t  turnRange: { startIndex: number; endIndex: number } | null;\n   394\t  sourceTurnIds: string[];\n   395\t  sourceArchiveEntryIds: string[];\n   396\t  title: string | null;\n   397\t  bodyText: string | null;\n   398\t  viewStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n   399\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n   400\t  updatedAt: string;\n   401\t}\n   402\t```\n   403\t\n   404\t### Routes\n   405\t\n   406\t| Operation | Method | Path | Service |\n   407\t|-----------|--------|------|---------|\n   408\t| Get process archive | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive` | `ArchiveReadService.getArchive` |\n   409\t| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\n   410\t| Get derived archive views | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` |\n   411\t| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views/refresh` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.refreshViews` |\n   412\t\n   413\tAll routes use existing actor resolution and `app.processAccessService` to\n   414\tenforce project/process access before archive services run.\n   415\t\n   416\t### Route Validation and Error Responses\n   417\t\n   418\t`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` should define these route schemas:\n   419\t\n   420\t- archive page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n   421\t- turn page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n   422\t- derived-view refresh body: empty object for Epic 7\n   423\t\n   424\tRoute responses:\n   425\t\n   426\t| Route | 200 | Errors |\n   427\t|-------|-----|--------|\n   428\t| `GET /archive` | `ArchivePage` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n   429\t| `GET /archive/turns` | `{ turns, page }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n   430\t| `GET /archive/derived-views` | `{ views }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n   431\t| `POST /archive/derived-views/refresh` | `{ views, refreshStatus }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `422` |\n   432\t\n   433\tError codes:\n   434\t\n   435\t| Status | Code | Meaning |\n   436\t|--------|------|---------|\n   437\t| 401 | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Actor is missing |\n   438\t| 403 | `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks project access |\n   439\t| 404 | `PROJECT_NOT_FOUND` | Project does not exist |\n   440\t| 404 | `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Process does not exist in project |\n   441\t| 409 | `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Derived-view refresh cannot safely reconcile with current archive state |\n   442\t| 422 | `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Cursor, limit, or derived-view refresh request is invalid |\n   443\t\n   444\t## Service Interfaces\n   445\t\n   446\t```typescript\n   447\texport interface ArchiveFinalizationService {\n   448\t  appendFinalizedEntry(args: {\n   449\t    projectId: string;\n   450\t    processId: string;\n   451\t    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n   452\t    finalizationKey: string;\n   453\t    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\n   454\t    bodyText?: string | null;\n   455\t    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\n   456\t    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\n   457\t    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\n   458\t    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\n   459\t    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\n   460\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\n   461\t\n   462\t  appendFromProcessHistoryItem(args: {\n   463\t    projectId: string;\n   464\t    processId: string;\n   465\t    historyItem: ProcessHistoryItem;\n   466\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry | null>;\n   467\t}\n   468\t\n   469\texport interface ArchiveReadService {\n   470\t  getArchive(args: {\n   471\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   472\t    projectId: string;\n   473\t    processId: string;\n   474\t    cursor?: string | null;\n   475\t    limit?: number;\n   476\t  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\n   477\t}\n   478\t\n   479\texport interface TurnDerivationService {\n   480\t  // Rebuilds cached turns by deterministic turnId rather than recreating\n   481\t  // opaque row ids, so downstream view provenance remains stable.\n   482\t  rebuildTurns(args: { projectId: string; processId: string }): Promise<DerivedTurn[]>;\n   483\t  getTurns(args: {\n   484\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   485\t    projectId: string;\n   486\t    processId: string;\n   487\t    cursor?: string | null;\n   488\t    limit?: number;\n   489\t  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\n   490\t}\n   491\t\n   492\texport interface DerivedArchiveViewService {\n   493\t  listViews(args: {\n   494\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n   495\t    projectId: string;\n   496\t    processId: string;\n   497\t  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[] }>;\n   498\t\n   499\t  refreshViews(args: {\n   500\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
