{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '501,760p'\"","aggregated_output":"   501\t    projectId: string;\n   502\t    processId: string;\n   503\t  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[]; refreshStatus: 'settled' | 'accepted' | 'degraded' }>;\n   504\t}\n   505\t```\n   506\t\n   507\t### PlatformStore Additions\n   508\t\n   509\t```typescript\n   510\texport interface PlatformStore {\n   511\t  appendArchiveEntry(args: {\n   512\t    projectId: string;\n   513\t    processId: string;\n   514\t    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n   515\t    finalizationKey: string;\n   516\t    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\n   517\t    bodyText?: string | null;\n   518\t    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\n   519\t    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\n   520\t    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\n   521\t    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\n   522\t    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\n   523\t    entryStatus?: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n   524\t    degradationReason?: string | null;\n   525\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\n   526\t\n   527\t  listArchiveEntries(args: {\n   528\t    processId: string;\n   529\t    cursor?: string | null;\n   530\t    limit: number;\n   531\t  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\n   532\t\n   533\t  upsertArchiveTurns(args: {\n   534\t    projectId: string;\n   535\t    processId: string;\n   536\t    turns: DerivedTurn[];\n   537\t  }): Promise<void>;\n   538\t\n   539\t  listArchiveTurns(args: {\n   540\t    processId: string;\n   541\t    cursor?: string | null;\n   542\t    limit: number;\n   543\t  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\n   544\t\n   545\t  replaceDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\n   546\t    projectId: string;\n   547\t    processId: string;\n   548\t    views: DerivedArchiveView[];\n   549\t  }): Promise<void>;\n   550\t\n   551\t  listDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\n   552\t    processId: string;\n   553\t  }): Promise<DerivedArchiveView[]>;\n   554\t}\n   555\t```\n   556\t\n   557\tConvex function validators should mirror these shapes directly. Fastify\n   558\tservices decide finalization, derivation, and refresh policy; `PlatformStore`\n   559\texposes only durable append/read/upsert/replace operations.\n   560\t\n   561\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\n   562\t\n   563\t### Flow 1: Capture Finalized Archive Entries\n   564\t\n   565\tThis flow covers the Story 1 primitive boundary behind AC-1.1 through AC-1.4.\n   566\tTrusted callers supply already-finalized archive-entry payloads to the durable\n   567\tappend/read primitive. Convex owns the canonical row shape, taxonomy\n   568\tvalidation, stable ordering, idempotency guard, related-id storage, and bounded\n   569\tprimitive reads.\n   570\t\n   571\t```mermaid\n   572\tsequenceDiagram\n   573\t    participant P as Trusted Caller\n   574\t    participant S as PlatformStore\n   575\t    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\n   576\t\n   577\t    P->>S: appendArchiveEntry(write)\n   578\t    Note over P,S: AC-1.1 finalized low-level entry payload\n   579\t    S->>X: appendArchiveEntry mutation\n   580\t    Note over S,X: AC-1.2/AC-1.3/AC-1.4 taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids\n   581\t    X-->>S: ArchiveEntry\n   582\t    S-->>P: ArchiveEntry\n   583\t```\n   584\t\n   585\t### Flow 2: Keep Live State Separate from Canonical Archive\n   586\t\n   587\tThis flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.3. Existing WebSocket upserts continue to\n   588\tserve active UI state through `process-live-normalizer.ts` and\n   589\t`process-live.ts`. Those live messages are not archive writes. Only completed\n   590\tobjects that reach a finalization point call `ArchiveFinalizationService`,\n   591\twhich maps finalized runtime/process objects into the Story 1 append primitive\n   592\texactly once.\n   593\t\n   594\tRetries are safe because every finalized object supplies a `finalizationKey`.\n   595\tExamples:\n   596\t\n   597\t- accepted user response: `response:${clientRequestId}`\n   598\t- runtime model message: `model:${sourceObjectId}`\n   599\t- tool call/result pair: `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:call` and `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:result`\n   600\t- process event: `event:${sourceObjectId}`\n   601\t\n   602\t### Flow 3: Read and Reopen Archive\n   603\t\n   604\tThis flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.4. The user reads archive entries through\n   605\tFastify routes under the existing process path. Archive reads do not depend on\n   606\tenvironment state or live WebSocket state. `ArchiveReadService` fetches one\n   607\tbounded page from Convex, applies route validation and access rules, and\n   608\treturns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\n   609\t\n   610\tThis flow owns displaying degraded entries already present in the response\n   611\tcontract. Deep artifact/source enrichment and lookup-failure degradation\n   612\tsemantics are added in Flow 6. Read-time degradation must not mutate the\n   613\tcanonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\n   614\tas degraded.\n   615\t\n   616\t### Flow 4: Derive Turns\n   617\t\n   618\tThis flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\n   619\tin ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\n   620\twhen refresh/rebuild is requested.\n   621\t\n   622\tGrouping rules:\n   623\t\n   624\t1. `user_message` starts a new turn.\n   625\t2. Entries before the first user message form turn `0` if they exist.\n   626\t3. `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`,\n   627\t   `tool_result`, and `process_event` attach to the active turn.\n   628\t  4. A `tool_result` with `relatedToolCallId` stays in the same turn as its\n   629\t   matching `tool_call` when both are present.\n   630\t  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\n   631\t\n   632\tRebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\n   633\tor explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\n   634\tstable `turnId` and `turnIndex`.\n   635\t\n   636\t### Flow 5: Produce Minimal Structural Views\n   637\t\n   638\tThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.5. Structural views are generated from\n   639\tturns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\n   640\t\n   641\t- `turn_range`: one contiguous range of turn indexes with source entry ids\n   642\t- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\n   643\t  context-management work\n   644\t\n   645\tNeither view contains model-generated summaries. `bodyText`, when present, is a\n   646\tdeterministic label or structural note such as `Turns 4-8`.\n   647\t\n   648\t### Flow 6: Connect Provenance\n   649\t\n   650\tThis flow covers AC-6.1 through AC-6.3. Archive entries store nullable related\n   651\tids. Building on the Flow 3 archive read surface, read services enrich when\n   652\tpossible:\n   653\t\n   654\t- artifact context through `PlatformStore.listArtifactVersions` or a targeted\n   655\t  artifact-version read helper\n   656\t- source context through Epic 6 `sourceProvenance` reads\n   657\t- tool context through `relatedToolCallId`\n   658\t\n   659\tIf a related record is unavailable, the entry remains visible. This flow owns\n   660\tthe artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\n   661\tstatus becomes `degraded` for the read response, or an enriched response\n   662\tincludes degraded related-context metadata without mutating the stored\n   663\tcanonical entry. Story 3 remains responsible for rendering that response\n   664\tstate to the user.\n   665\t\n   666\t### Flow 7: Return Later and Bound Long Reads\n   667\t\n   668\tThis flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\n   669\tviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\n   670\tpagination with default limits:\n   671\t\n   672\t- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n   673\t- turns: default 50, max 100\n   674\t- derived views: default 50\n   675\t\n   676\tA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\n   677\treturn degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\n   678\tavailable.\n   679\t\n   680\t## Implementation Chunks\n   681\t\n   682\t| Chunk | Story | Scope | ACs | Primary Tests |\n   683\t|-------|-------|-------|-----|---------------|\n   684\t| 0 | Foundation | Contracts, Convex schema, fixtures, error codes, compatibility mapping skeletons | All support | Relevant sections: API Contracts, Data Model. Non-TC: archive contract vocabulary and finalized-only schema test |\n   685\t| 1 | Archive persistence | Append/read entries, taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids | AC-1.x | Relevant sections: Flow 1, Data Model. Non-TC: atomic sequence assignment and primitive idempotency |\n   686\t| 2 | Finalization boundary | Completion hooks, live/archive separation, retry idempotency | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, Service Interfaces. Non-TC: live-history separation, compatibility mapping decision |\n   687\t| 3 | Archive read/reopen | Routes, access controls, empty state, bounded page contract, environment-loss reads, degraded-entry display | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Route Validation. Non-TC: invalid archive request handling |\n   688\t| 4 | Turn derivation | Deterministic grouping, cached rebuild, degraded turns | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model. Non-TC: turn-zero grouping, rebuild stability |\n   689\t| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\n   690\t| 6 | Provenance coherence | Artifact/source enrichment and related-record lookup degradation semantics | AC-6.x | Relevant sections: Flow 6, API Contracts. Non-TC: none |\n   691\t| 7 | Reopen/bounded reads | Reload behavior, derived failures, long-process pagination hardening | AC-7.x | Relevant sections: Flow 7, Route Validation. Non-TC: none |\n   692\t\n   693\t## Verification\n   694\t\n   695\t| Script | Command | Use |\n   696\t|--------|---------|-----|\n   697\t| `red-verify` | `pnpm run red-verify` | After skeleton and Red tests |\n   698\t| `verify` | `pnpm run verify` | Standard development gate |\n   699\t| `green-verify` | `pnpm run green-verify` | After implementation passes tests |\n   700\t| `verify-all` | `pnpm run verify-all` | Story/Epic completion |\n   701\t\n   702\t## Deferred Items\n   703\t\n   704\t| Item | Related AC | Reason Deferred | Future Work |\n   705\t|------|------------|-----------------|-------------|\n   706\t| Historical migration/backfill from `processHistoryItems` | A7 | Epic 7 starts forward canonical archive and compatibility bridge | Later migration if needed |\n   707\t| Model-generated summaries | Scope, AC-5.x | Structural views only | Later context-management epic |\n   708\t| Model-specific prompt packing | Scope | Not required for archive truth | Later context-management epic |\n   709\t| External-source archive integration | Scope | Epic 6/7 sequence is repository-focused | Later source-integration work |\n   710\t\n   711\t## Resolved Implementation Decisions\n   712\t\n   713\t| Decision | Applied In |\n   714\t|----------|------------|\n   715\t| `relatedSourceProvenanceId` is implemented as the stable Epic 6 provenance identifier and stays string-shaped in shared contracts unless cross-table typing becomes frictionless. | Chunk 6 |\n   716\t| Turn cache rebuild happens on turn/derived-view read or explicit refresh, not on every archive append. | Chunk 4 |\n   717\t| Compatibility mapping does not publish archive entries back into the live history stream. Live history publisher remains unchanged. | Chunk 2 |\n   718\t\n   719\t## Self-Review Checklist\n   720\t\n   721\t- [x] Every Epic 7 AC has a module owner.\n   722\t- [x] Every Epic 7 Tech Design Question is answered.\n   723\t- [x] Canonical archive and live upserts stay separate.\n   724\t- [x] Turns and derived views are rebuildable, not canonical.\n   725\t- [x] Structural views exclude generated summaries.\n   726\t- [x] Verification commands use project scripts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
